     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it might be a mistake. Can you confirm what you meant?\n\n**The issue:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose for adults is **800 mg**. This order is 1600 mg per dose, twice that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults is **3200 mg/day**. This order is twice that too.\n- At this dose, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other NSAID toxicity goes up a lot, especially for an older inpatient.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). If 1600 was meant as the daily total, this is the closest match.\n2. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day), the maximum standard dose.\n3. **600 mg four times daily** (2400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose.\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, for example under a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying the above-maximum dose was confirmed by the attending. Otherwise, give me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
